# The in-mesh WARNING debt the embedded Doc tree carries, for `mw-plugin-test compile
# --warning-baseline`. Format: `<NodeType path> <diagnostic id>`, `#` comments, blanks ignored.
#
# ── THIS FILE IS DELIBERATELY EMPTY OF ENTRIES ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# An EMPTY baseline is the strictest setting there is, and it is spelled as an empty FILE on
# purpose: nothing is tolerated, so EVERY in-mesh warning this tree produces fails the bake. It is
# not the same as omitting `--warning-baseline`, which would be OBSERVE-ONLY — "no known debt" and
# "the bake never read a baseline" must never render the same, which is why the file stays here
# rather than being deleted. `bake-then-gate.sh` asserts both ratchets print ENFORCED.
#
# 🚨 SHRINK-ONLY: an unlisted (type, code) pair FAILS the bake, and a listed pair whose type
# compiled clean of that code is STALE and FAILS it until the line is deleted. A listed type that
# did not compile this run is UNVERIFIABLE, never stale. With no lines at all, the first half is
# the whole contract: any warning, anywhere in this tree, is an error.
#
# ── WHERE THE SEVEN LINES WENT (2026-09-18) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# They were NOT fixed by writing anything, and they were not swept away either. Every one of them
# named CS1591 or CS1701 — the two families #4591 added to `CompileWarning.NotReported`, the
# in-mesh compile's PARITY list, so that in-mesh C# is held to the standard `src/` C# is held to
# rather than a stricter one. A raw CSharpCompilation applies no NoWarn at all; those two families
# are the ones no `dotnet build` in this fleet reports, so the in-mesh compile had been the only
# compiler in the fleet still reporting them.
#
# The tester names such a line INERT: it tolerates nothing (nothing can produce the code) and hides
# nothing, and it prints "Delete the lines" on every run. Deleting them is that instruction carried
# out, and it leaves the file exactly consistent with what the bake measures.
#
# Measured on this tree at e8fce8130d, with `MW_LOG_LEVEL=Information`:
#
#   before  warnings: 0 raw occurrence(s) folded to 0 distinct site(s), over 0 of 4 compiled type(s)
#           warnings: 7 INERT baseline entr(ies) naming CS1591, CS1701 — … Delete the lines.
#           warnings: warnings     ratchet — ENFORCED against 0 baseline entr(ies): 0 NEW, 0 stale
#           warnings: doc-comments ratchet — ENFORCED against 0 baseline entr(ies): 0 NEW, 0 stale
#   after   the same three measured lines, and no INERT line.
#
# Both ratchets were already enforcing against ZERO entries before the trim — `WarningBaseline.For`
# excludes a retired code — so nothing this file used to say was being relied on by anything. The
# tree itself produces NO warnings at all: 4 of 4 NodeTypes compile clean.
#
# 🚨 What this file is NOT. It is not a record that the Doc tree's public members are documented —
# CS1591 is suppressed, so nobody is measuring that. Writing those doc comments is worth doing and
# changes NO verdict here; do not read an empty file as a claim that it was done.
#
# 🚨 ADD A LINE ONLY FOR A WARNING A RUN ACTUALLY REPORTED, and prefer fixing it. The rules, the two
# ratchets, the parity list and the three diagnostic codes that were fixed at the ROOT rather than
# baselined are documented once, in Doc/Architecture/InMeshWarningStandard.
